# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every host.
#
# Windows' git defaults to `core.autocrlf=true` (GitHub's windows-latest runner included), which
# checks text out with CRLF. The repository reads its own sources as data — the mutation
# catalogue's multi-line `find` patterns, the runtime-parity check's `fn runtime() -> Str` lines in
# compiler/emit.nz, golden outputs, the compiler's own sources — and all of it is LF in the index,
# so a CRLF checkout fails `cargo xtask check` and the tests on Windows alone (CI 2026-10-16).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Line endings that are the point of the file: fixtures for the lexer's CRLF handling and inputs
# with a carriage return inside them, kept byte for byte.
toolchain/frontend-tests/inputs/lex/crlf.nz -text
toolchain/frontend-tests/inputs/lex/raw.nz -text
toolchain/commands/tests/inputs/only-comment.nz -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md -text
